comment0.target=Paddle
comment0.text=\n\ A\ paddle\ is\ an\ object\ that\ goes\ back\ and\ forth.\ Though\ it\ would\ be\ nice\ if\ balls\ would\ bounce\ of\ it.\n\ \n\ @author\ The\ teachers\ \n\ @version\ 1\n
comment1.params=width\ height
comment1.target=Paddle(int,\ int)
comment1.text=\n\ Constructs\ a\ new\ paddle\ with\ the\ given\ dimensions.\n
comment2.params=
comment2.target=void\ act()
comment2.text=\n\ Act\ -\ do\ whatever\ the\ Paddle\ wants\ to\ do.\ This\ method\ is\ called\ whenever\n\ the\ 'Act'\ or\ 'Run'\ button\ gets\ pressed\ in\ the\ environment.\n
comment3.params=
comment3.target=void\ changeDirection()
comment3.text=\n\ Will\ rotate\ the\ paddle\ 180\ degrees\ if\ the\ paddle\ is\ at\ worlds\ edge.\n
comment4.params=
comment4.target=void\ createImage()
comment4.text=\n\ Vi\ s\u00E6tter\ Paddel\ til\ et\ nyt\ billede.\n\ Efter\ dette\ definere\ vi\ nu\ image\ p\u00E5\ linje\ 67\ ,s\u00E5ledes\ at\ vi\ p\u00E5\ linje\ 68\ kan\ bruge\ Greenfoot\ kommandoen\ scale\ til\ at\ give\ Paddlen\ den\ rigtige\n\ width\ og\ height.\n\ Dette\ g\u00F8res\ ogs\u00E5\ for,\ PaddelTwo,\ Ball\ og\ PingWorld.\n
